# devices: duo
# visual-review: inspect all inner-display captures: side posture keeps pills in the vertical bar, upright uses the composer row; check order, clipping and the task roster without treating launch fixtures as native tap coverage.
# Unfolded iPhone Duo only: run with
#   scripts/wonderctl --device duo run apps/ios/control/duo-unfolded/bar-pills.wctl
# Captures explicitly select the inner display in both orientations.
# Unfolded with the bar down the side (`orient portrait`: wide, as the owner
# holds it), the composer's pills sit in the system's vertical bar under the
# sidebar button, as on the folded cover; the composer has no pill row. Upright,
# iOS puts the status bar across the top and the pills stay in the row. Bar
# items are not found by id, so check the inner-display capture. No taps
# (#387). Nothing is sent.
hinge 180
orient portrait
launch --fixture read-preview --fixture send-preview --fixture activity-preview --fixture response-turn-diff-preview --fixture files-preview --fixture project-files-conversation-preview
wait --id message-draft --timeout 30
shot duo-bar-pills-side --display primary-1
orient landscape-right
wait --id message-draft --timeout 30
shot duo-bar-pills-upright --display primary-1
orient portrait

# The roster opens from its own pill at launch; no Duo taps or model work.
launch --fixture subagent-fixture --fixture chat-layout --fixture chat-layout-unsaved --fixture project-subagents --fixture project-claude-tasks --fixture open-project-thread --fixture task-roster-open --fixture task-roster-in-bar
wait --id message-draft --timeout 30
wait --id project-subagent-roster-list --timeout 20
shot duo-bar-pills-roster-side --display primary-1
orient landscape-right
wait --id project-subagent-roster-list --timeout 20
shot duo-bar-pills-roster-upright --display primary-1
# Leave a known cover posture for the next scenario.
hinge 0
orient portrait
